  m_Name: LionHead
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-lionhead
  DisplayIndex: 15
  DisplayName: The lion's mouth
  Shape: 14
  TeachingHint: Leave the mane. Roll between the eyes, around the muzzle and into
    the green mouth.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 5668339104532114420, guid: c2cf29096073b4d8595ba93de69f7f16, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: A dry bronze-and-glass lion-head container under Earth gravity.
    Its jagged mane and ears are the real enclosure boundary. The bevelled eyes,
    nose and muzzle are fixed physical obstacles. From the upper-left mane, move
    to the forehead, pass between the eyes, turn around either cheek and reach the
    circular mouth exit. Face colouring and mane inlays are optical decoration, not
    invisible walls. The same steel sphere, contacts and rotation controls are used.
    Shared exit assist pulls the ball through an unobstructed opening within 40 mm.
    This is deliberate gameplay assistance; the entire sphere must still physically
    clear the bore before completion.
